I play badminton every Thursday evening.
Kasper and Sara play on the same team as me.
Tomorrow is Friday, and I have invited them over for dinner.
I want to cook a traditional Danish dish.
So I decide to make meatballs with potatoes.
I find a good recipe on the internet.
Now I need to write a shopping list.
First, I need meat for the meatballs.
The recipe says five hundred grams of minced pork.
Then I also need two large yellow onions.
I also note down one deciliter of milk and an egg.
I write it all down on my notepad.
Afterwards, I look at the amount of potatoes.
I must buy exactly one kilo of small potatoes.
Finally, I add butter and salt to the list.
You must always use plenty of butter to fry the meat.
The list is finally complete, and I am ready.
Tomorrow after work, I will go straight to the supermarket.
